  "discussion": "A small, short period north-northeast swell will fill in today, maintaining small surf along north-facing shores. A larger, long- period northwest swell will begin to arrive late Saturday, pushing north and exposed west shore surf above the High Surf Advisory threshold Sunday into Monday. The swell will shift slightly more northerly and may briefly build further on Monday before dropping Tuesday. A small, medium period south swell will peak today, then gradually decline through the weekend. During the first half of next week, south shore surf will return to below seasonal averages. Surf along most east-facing shores will rise slightly today due to wrap from the north and southerly swells. Additionally, east- facing shorelines exposed to the larger north swell Sunday night into Monday will have the potential for advisory level surf during that time.",
